# ---- chapter 1: the duke who hoped
('c1a',N,"Florence... fifteen thirteen.","Florence... 1513."),
('c1b',N,"Niccolo Machiavelli has lost his government job. He has been jailed... and tortured. Now he lives on a small farm outside the city... writing a short book about power.","Niccolò Machiavelli has lost his government job. He has been jailed... and tortured. Now he lives on a small farm outside the city... writing a short book about power."),
('c1c',N,"He calls it The Prince. And one of its main characters... is a man he had watched up close. Cesare Borgia.","He calls it The Prince. And one of its main characters... is a man he had watched up close. Cesare Borgia."),
('c1d',N,"Borgia's father was Pope Alexander the Sixth. With his father's power behind him... Borgia built a state of his own.","Borgia's father was Pope Alexander VI. With his father's power behind him... Borgia built a state of his own."),
('c1e',N,"Then, in the summer of fifteen oh three... his father died. And Borgia himself was so sick... he was close to death.","Then, in the summer of 1503... his father died. And Borgia himself was so sick... he was close to death."),
('c1f',N,"Machiavelli says Borgia told him he had planned for everything his father's death could bring... everything, except being close to death himself.","Machiavelli says Borgia told him he had planned for everything his father's death could bring... everything, except being close to death himself."),
('c1g',N,"Now Rome had to choose a new Pope. Borgia could not pick the winner... but he could still block one.","Now Rome had to choose a new Pope. Borgia could not pick the winner... but he could still block one."),
('c1h',N,"And he let a man through. A cardinal he had injured in the past... a man with every reason to fear him. That man became Pope Julius the Second.","And he let a man through. A cardinal he had injured in the past... a man with every reason to fear him. That man became Pope Julius II."),
('c1i',N,"Why would Borgia allow it? Because he hoped. He hoped fresh favours would wash away old wounds.","Why would Borgia allow it? Because he hoped. He hoped fresh favours would wash away old wounds."),
('q1',Q,"Machiavelli's answer is ice cold. He who believes that new benefits will cause great personages to forget old injuries... is deceived.","Machiavelli's answer is ice cold. \"He who believes that new benefits will cause great personages to forget old injuries is deceived.\""),
('q1b',Q,"And his verdict on Borgia? The duke erred in his choice... and it was the cause of his ultimate ruin.","And his verdict on Borgia? \"The duke erred in his choice, and it was the cause of his ultimate ruin.\""),
('c1k',N,"Look at what the mistake really was. Not cruelty. Not weakness. Wishful thinking.","Look at what the mistake really was. Not cruelty. Not weakness. Wishful thinking."),
('q2',Q,'Machiavelli explains it in one line. For men injure either from fear or hatred.','Machiavelli explains it in one line. "For men injure either from fear or hatred."'),
('c1m',N,'Someone you once hurt... may still resent you, or fear you. And resentment, handed power, tends to strike first.','Someone you once hurt... may still resent you, or fear you. And resentment, handed power, tends to strike first.'),
('c1n',N,"Picture an office. Last year, Maya took credit for a teammate's idea... in front of everyone.","Picture an office. Last year, Maya took credit for a teammate's idea... in front of everyone."),
('c1o',N,"This year, she's friendly. Coffee. Compliments. A birthday card.","This year, she's friendly. Coffee. Compliments. A birthday card."),
('c1p',N,"Then a promotion opens up... and that teammate sits on the hiring panel.","Then a promotion opens up... and that teammate sits on the hiring panel."),
('c1q',N,"Does a birthday card erase that meeting? Machiavelli would say... don't bet your future on it.","Does a birthday card erase that meeting? Machiavelli would say... don't bet your future on it."),
('c1r',N,"His lesson isn't revenge. It's clear sight. Know who you have hurt. Repair it honestly... or prepare for it. But never just hope.","His lesson isn't revenge. It's clear sight. Know who you have hurt. Repair it honestly... or prepare for it. But never just hope."),
# ---- chapter 2: a ladder built by enemies
('c2a',N,"Machiavelli has a second idea about enemies. And this one... is strangely hopeful.","Machiavelli has a second idea about enemies. And this one... is strangely hopeful."),
('c2b',N,"In chapter twenty, he writes that leaders become great by overcoming what stands against them. Fortune even sends a new leader enemies... so that he can rise.","In chapter 20, he writes that leaders become great by overcoming what stands against them. Fortune even sends a new leader enemies... so that he can rise."),
('q3',Q,"By them to mount higher... as by a ladder which his enemies have raised.","\"…by them to mount higher, as by a ladder which his enemies have raised.\""),
('c2c',N,"Read that again. Every person who doubted you... every door that was shut in your face... can become a rung.","Read that again. Every person who doubted you... every door that was shut in your face... can become a rung."),
('c2d',N,"A girl is cut from her school's basketball team. The coach says she's too slow.","A girl is cut from her school's basketball team. The coach says she's too slow."),
('c2e',N,"That sentence becomes her alarm clock. Five in the morning. Every day. For a year.","That sentence becomes her alarm clock. 5 a.m. Every day. For a year."),
('c2f',N,"Next season, she makes the team. The coach never trained her... but he built the ladder.","Next season, she makes the team. The coach never trained her... but he built the ladder."),
('c2g',N,"And Machiavelli goes one step further. He noticed that new rulers often found more loyalty in people they first distrusted... than in the ones they trusted from the start.","And Machiavelli goes one step further. He noticed that new rulers often found more loyalty in people they first distrusted... than in the ones they trusted from the start."),
('c2h',N,"Why? Because a former rival who joins you has something to prove. They have to show, by what they do... that you were wrong about them.","Why? Because a former rival who joins you has something to prove. They have to show, by what they do... that you were wrong about them."),
('c2i',N,"So today's opponent could be tomorrow's most loyal partner... if you leave the door open.","So today's opponent could be tomorrow's most loyal partner... if you leave the door open."),
# ---- chapter 3: the sword in the sand (Rumi)
('c3a',N,"Now... travel east. To Rumi.","Now... travel east. To Rumi."),
('c3b',N,"In the thirteenth century, he wrote the Masnavi... a vast poem, full of stories.","In the 13th century, he wrote the Masnavi... a vast poem, full of stories."),
('c3c',N,"One of them is about Ali, the great warrior of early Islam... whom the story calls the Lion of God.","One of them is about Ali, the great warrior of early Islam... whom the story calls the Lion of God."),
('c3d',N,"Ali is locked in a fight with an enemy chief. And Ali is winning. The fight is almost over.","Ali is locked in a fight with an enemy chief. And Ali is winning. The fight is almost over."),
('c3e',N,"Then the beaten man does the one thing he has left. He spits in Ali's face.","Then the beaten man does the one thing he has left. He spits in Ali's face."),
('c3f',N,"Stop the story right there. Every instinct says... strike. Anyone watching would understand.","Stop the story right there. Every instinct says... strike. Anyone watching would understand."),
('q4',Q,"But as Whinfield's translation tells it... Ali, instead of taking vengeance on him, at once dropped his sword... to the Magian's great astonishment.",'But as Whinfield\'s translation tells it... "Ali, instead of taking vengeance on him, at once dropped his sword, to the Magian\'s great astonishment."'),
('c3g',N,"The enemy can't believe it. Why spare me? Why now... right after I insulted you?","The enemy can't believe it. Why spare me? Why now... right after I insulted you?"),
('c3h',N,"In essence, Ali's answer is this. He fought for something higher than himself... not for his own pride.","In essence, Ali's answer is this. He fought for something higher than himself... not for his own pride."),
('c3i',N,"The moment that spit made it personal, anger had entered the fight. And a fight run by anger... was not one he was willing to win.","The moment that spit made it personal, anger had entered the fight. And a fight run by anger... was not one he was willing to win."),
('c3j',N,"The story says that one act won what the sword never could. The enemy chief... and his whole family... came over to Ali's faith.","The story says that one act won what the sword never could. The enemy chief... and his whole family... came over to Ali's faith."),
('c3k',N,"Now look at that spit again. It was a weapon... the last one the enemy had.","Now look at that spit again. It was a weapon... the last one the enemy had."),
('c3l',N,"He couldn't win the fight anymore. So he tried to win Ali's temper.","He couldn't win the fight anymore. So he tried to win Ali's temper."),
('c3m',N,"If Ali had struck in rage, the enemy would still have been in control of him... for one final second.","If Ali had struck in rage, the enemy would still have been in control of him... for one final second."),
('c3n',N,"That's Rumi's point. The enemy in front of you is beaten in a moment. The anger inside you... keeps fighting long after.","That's Rumi's point. The enemy in front of you is beaten in a moment. The anger inside you... keeps fighting long after."),
# ---- chapter 4: mind vs heart
('c4a',N,"So who is right? The cold strategist... or the poet?","So who is right? The cold strategist... or the poet?"),
('c4b',N,'At first, they sound like opposites. Machiavelli says, never assume an old injury is forgotten. Rumi says, drop the sword.','At first, they sound like opposites. Machiavelli says, never assume an old injury is forgotten. Rumi says, drop the sword.'),
('c4c',N,"But look closer. Borgia lost because he let hope make his decision. Ali won because he refused to let anger make his.","But look closer. Borgia lost because he let hope make his decision. Ali won because he refused to let anger make his."),
('c4d',N,"Same lesson... from two sides. When an enemy is near, don't let a feeling take the wheel.","Same lesson... from two sides. When an enemy is near, don't let a feeling take the wheel."),
('c4e',N,"Machiavelli is the mind. See your enemy exactly as they are. Not better. Not worse.","Machiavelli is the mind. See your enemy exactly as they are. Not better. Not worse."),
('c4f',N,"Rumi is the heart. See yourself exactly as you are... and notice the moment a fight becomes about your pride.","Rumi is the heart. See yourself exactly as you are... and notice the moment a fight becomes about your pride."),
('c4g',N,"A message from a rival lands at midnight. Sharp. Built to sting.","A message from a rival lands at midnight. Sharp. Built to sting."),
('c4h',N,"The mind asks... what can this person really do to me? The heart asks... what does my anger want me to do? And whose plan is that?","The mind asks... what can this person really do to me? The heart asks... what does my anger want me to do? And whose plan is that?"),
('c4i',N,"Most of the time... the angry reply is exactly the move they were hoping you'd make.","Most of the time... the angry reply is exactly the move they were hoping you'd make."),
